1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,300
Welcome to Xmip.

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:07,230
Xmip stands for Cross OS Messaging & Integration Platform.

3
00:00:07,410 --> 00:00:12,385
It is an open-source messaging and integration platform written in Rust.

4
00:00:12,565 --> 00:00:19,140
It is on premises first and cloud installable, so organizations choose where their integration runs.

5
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:27,145
This is the Xmip project story: what it connects, how it records responsibility, and how people design and operate it.

6
00:00:29,325 --> 00:00:36,750
Xmip is being developed for organizations that need dependable messaging and integration under their own control.

7
00:00:36,930 --> 00:00:44,430
It carries forward familiar integration concepts while putting deployment and data under organizational control.

8
00:00:44,610 --> 00:00:53,510
Its central promise is accountability: once a message is accepted, its journey and outcome give operators evidence they can act on.

9
00:00:55,690 --> 00:01:01,465
For a CEO, the question is what happens to the business when a system exchange stops.

10
00:01:01,645 --> 00:01:07,070
Xmip focuses on accountable outcomes, recovery and organizational choice.

11
00:01:07,250 --> 00:01:14,225
A practical evaluation connects those principles to a real process, its owner and its business impact.

12
00:01:16,405 --> 00:01:21,605
For a CIO, Xmip keeps infrastructure decisions within the organization.

13
00:01:21,785 --> 00:01:28,185
Nodes can be placed close to systems, at remote sites or on chosen hosting infrastructure.

14
00:01:28,365 --> 00:01:36,265
Open implementation and recorded architecture make it possible to assess the platform and understand how it evolves.

15
00:01:38,445 --> 00:01:43,320
Consider an illustrative order travelling from a sales system to a warehouse.

16
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:48,175
A Receive Location accepts the stream, and Xmip persists a message.

17
00:01:48,355 --> 00:01:53,105
Matching subscriptions open journeys to the destinations that want it.

18
00:01:53,285 --> 00:01:57,135
A Send Location attempts delivery to the warehouse.

19
00:01:57,315 --> 00:02:02,615
That journey gives an interrupted exchange a place and an outcome to investigate.

20
00:02:04,795 --> 00:02:08,070
Acceptance is the handover of responsibility.

21
00:02:08,250 --> 00:02:10,825
Before it, the sender owns the stream.

22
00:02:11,005 --> 00:02:14,930
After it, Xmip persists a message and records its progress.

23
00:02:15,110 --> 00:02:23,085
Keeping refusal distinct from a later delivery failure helps both organizations understand which side should act next.

24
00:02:25,265 --> 00:02:29,565
A subscription expresses which messages a destination wants.

25
00:02:29,745 --> 00:02:35,395
Each match opens a journey, while an unmatched message remains available for replay.

26
00:02:35,575 --> 00:02:43,400
Operators can pause a subscription without discarding its work, then resume the held messages in the order they arrived.

27
00:02:45,580 --> 00:02:47,830
Recovery starts with the outcome.

28
00:02:48,010 --> 00:02:51,160
A routing issue calls for correction and replay.

29
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:57,665
A failed delivery calls for investigation and retry, or an intentional dismissal.

30
00:02:57,845 --> 00:03:04,920
Xmip keeps those actions distinct, while configured attempts and backoff handle repeated delivery attempts.

31
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:11,050
An Xmip Application describes the integration itself.

32
00:03:11,230 --> 00:03:16,380
A binding places that application on a node and supplies its environment.

33
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:26,560
This separation lets developers reason about the business exchange while deployment choices determine which systems, addresses and machines participate.

34
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:32,890
Configuration in Visual Studio Code is a flex moment.

35
00:03:33,070 --> 00:03:37,970
Text editing and graphical designers work with the same configuration.

36
00:03:38,150 --> 00:03:48,750
Completion, validation and reference-aware renaming help developers make consistent changes, while Xmip’s language server supplies the rules behind the design.

37
00:03:50,930 --> 00:03:53,280
TOML is another flex moment.

38
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:59,585
Xmip configuration stays in readable text that teams can version, compare and review.

39
00:03:59,765 --> 00:04:02,290
The designer works with that same source.

40
00:04:02,470 --> 00:04:09,020
This makes configuration an engineering artifact the team can understand and maintain together.

41
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:15,250
Some exchanges need business steps as well as delivery.

42
00:04:15,430 --> 00:04:22,655
Xmip models these as Work Processes, designed in BPMN and compiled into executable units.

43
00:04:22,835 --> 00:04:27,485
Their state belongs to the ledger, so waiting work does not hold a thread.

44
00:04:27,665 --> 00:04:36,065
Compilation and execution exist as components; connecting them into the assembled service remains a project milestone.

45
00:04:38,245 --> 00:04:44,545
Xmip separates how data travels, how it is represented, and what the integration does with it.

46
00:04:44,725 --> 00:04:50,075
Contracts define acceptance rules, while processing expresses business flow.

47
00:04:50,255 --> 00:04:57,080
Providers extend individual capabilities through explicit interfaces and a versioned C boundary.

48
00:04:57,260 --> 00:05:03,810
That modular architecture lets the platform evolve without treating every change as a replacement.

49
00:05:05,990 --> 00:05:14,490
Xmip’s technology estate spans file transfer, web communication, message brokers, databases and industrial systems.

50
00:05:14,670 --> 00:05:22,770
SFTP, HTTP, AMQP, Kafka, PostgreSQL and OPC UA are examples of that scope.

51
00:05:22,950 --> 00:05:26,275
A site build chooses the technologies it needs.

52
00:05:26,455 --> 00:05:33,505
This is the estate’s breadth, with availability depending on the capability and its integration into the service.

53
00:05:35,685 --> 00:05:38,385
Trust is explicit at Xmip’s boundaries.

54
00:05:38,565 --> 00:05:46,865
Parties carry identities, receive locations define what they accept, and outbound exchanges use their own identity.

55
00:05:47,045 --> 00:05:55,920
Certificate authentication, protected storage connections and encrypted embedded data give that architecture concrete foundations.

56
00:05:58,100 --> 00:06:01,175
Xmip Storage gives work a persistent home.

57
00:06:01,355 --> 00:06:08,330
A small deployment can host storage within its own node, while other nodes reach it over mutual TLS.

58
00:06:08,510 --> 00:06:15,210
The ledger holds messages, journeys and pending work, separate from administration and audit concerns.

59
00:06:17,390 --> 00:06:21,490
A deployment is a composition of roles and capabilities.

60
00:06:21,670 --> 00:06:30,220
Executing brings the message stages together in one process, while other roles serve storage, observation and operation.

61
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:36,850
Site builds select the target and technologies; configuration determines what the node starts.

62
00:06:39,030 --> 00:06:42,955
Cross-operating-system working is a shared flex moment.

63
00:06:43,135 --> 00:06:49,210
Xmip’s architecture targets Windows, Linux and Mac computers with one integration model.

64
00:06:49,390 --> 00:06:55,915
Site builds select the roles and technologies for a developer machine, an edge gateway or a server.

65
00:06:56,095 --> 00:07:00,620
Packaging and validation progress separately on each platform.

66
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:06,200
Offline operation is part of Xmip’s design.

67
00:07:06,380 --> 00:07:12,955
Packages can be prepared where dependencies are reachable, then brought into disconnected environments.

68
00:07:13,135 --> 00:07:21,935
Internet access is an explicit capability, supporting sites where connectivity is restricted, intermittent or deliberately absent.

69
00:07:24,115 --> 00:07:31,940
Operators can choose a command line, PowerShell, desktop or web interface without learning a different platform model.

70
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:35,320
The same scopes and meanings guide investigation.

71
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:42,050
Automation and visual inspection become different ways to work with the same operational evidence.

72
00:07:44,230 --> 00:07:48,530
Operations in your phone is a flex moment in Xmip’s design.

73
00:07:48,710 --> 00:07:55,660
The mobile host brings the same cluster health and scope navigation to Android and iPhone targets.

74
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:59,290
It follows nodes remotely in the Observer role.

75
00:07:59,470 --> 00:08:07,945
Device validation remains a project milestone, while the principle stays the same: understand the affected scope wherever you are.

76
00:08:10,125 --> 00:08:13,600
Health should tell an operator where to look and what to do.

77
00:08:13,780 --> 00:08:17,430
Xmip uses named conditions and scope navigation.

78
00:08:17,610 --> 00:08:26,835
A parent holding points into its children, where the affected resource and its reason help distinguish a deliberate pause from strain or failure.

79
00:08:29,015 --> 00:08:32,965
Current observation and audit answer different questions.

80
00:08:33,145 --> 00:08:36,145
Observation shows what is happening now.

81
00:08:36,325 --> 00:08:39,775
Audit records actions and outcomes over time.

82
00:08:39,955 --> 00:08:50,230
Chained program records, verification and journey evidence help the team investigate a specific exchange instead of guessing from disconnected symptoms.

83
00:08:52,410 --> 00:08:57,685
Xmip also exposes read-only access through the Model Context Protocol.

84
00:08:57,865 --> 00:09:03,915
Clients can inspect health, measurements, audit and journeys through tools and scoped resources.

85
00:09:04,095 --> 00:09:12,920
The behavior follows the command line, and each answer is audited, keeping observation connected to established operational controls.

86
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:21,050
Open source is a flex moment because teams can inspect, improve and extend Xmip.

87
00:09:21,230 --> 00:09:28,105
The platform is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version three or later.

88
00:09:28,285 --> 00:09:33,885
Recorded architecture and explicit capability interfaces support that freedom.

89
00:09:34,065 --> 00:09:40,940
Independent modules loaded across the documented boundary can use their publisher’s chosen license.

90
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:48,470
The engineering approach connects decisions to implementation and verification.

91
00:09:48,650 --> 00:09:56,925
Capability boundaries make ownership clear, while the Essentials and test harnesses exercise behavior and expose evidence.

92
00:09:57,105 --> 00:10:04,680
For the project team, progress means a demonstrated flow and reproducible results, alongside the design.

93
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:10,410
Xmip Continuum is the active development stream.

94
00:10:10,590 --> 00:10:16,065
The working foundation covers messaging, recovery, storage and program audit.

95
00:10:16,245 --> 00:10:23,320
Next milestones bring the broader components into the assembled service and complete deployment validation.

96
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:28,150
Linear names the product release model; no Linear release has shipped yet.

97
00:10:30,330 --> 00:10:40,280
Xmip brings the story together: connect systems under your control, define the exchange in readable configuration, and follow its recorded outcome.

98
00:10:40,460 --> 00:10:44,610
Leaders assess business continuity and infrastructure choice.

99
00:10:44,790 --> 00:10:48,665
Developers work in TOML and Visual Studio Code.

100
00:10:48,845 --> 00:10:55,070
Operators follow health, messages and journeys to investigate and recover the exchange.

101
00:10:55,250 --> 00:10:58,400
That is the platform this project is building.
